**Figure 1.** OLS straight-line fit to n = 40 simulated points (x = 0..39; y = 2.5 + 0.8x + e, e ~ N(0, 3^2), numpy default_rng(217)). Solid line: fitted line; shaded band: 95% confidence interval for the mean line (t, 38 df); dashed: the true line. Slope 0.814 (95% CI 0.728 to 0.900), intercept 1.91 (95% CI -0.03 to 3.86), R^2 = 0.907. Both intervals contain the true values (0.8, 2.5). Note the shaded band is the CI for the line, not a prediction interval, so most points lie outside it.

